Domain Name and DNS Setup
After the website was working through the Azure public IP address, I purchased a custom domain name from Namecheap.

The domain name used for this project was:

arinmehla.info

The domain was configured to point to the Azure virtual machine public IP address:

20.92.249.85

The domain was tested using:

ping arinmehla.info

The output showed that the domain resolved to the correct public IP address:

arinmehla.info (20.92.249.85)

Although the ping command showed 100% packet loss, this did not mean the website was down. The domain was resolving correctly, and the website was successfully tested using HTTPS. ICMP ping can be blocked by cloud firewall or network rules, so curl was used as the main website test.


HTTPS/SSL Configuration

HTTPS was configured so that the website could be accessed securely.
The HTTPS website was tested using:

curl -I https://arinmehla.info

The successful output was:

HTTP/1.1 200 OK

Server: nginx/1.24.0 (Ubuntu)

Content-Type: text/html

Content-Length: 3956

This confirmed that the website was accessible through HTTPS.

The HTTP version was also tested:

curl -I http://arinmehla.info

The output showed:

HTTP/1.1 301 Moved Permanently

Location: https://arinmehla.info/

This confirmed that normal HTTP traffic redirects to the secure HTTPS version of the website.
